From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: clamp autotuner to GMEM on A7xx to eliminate runtime sampling stutter

On Adreno 7xx, dynamic autotuning samples hardware performance counters to
experiment with GMEM vs Sysmem passes. On the Snapdragon 8s Gen 3, switching
to Sysmem causes heavy SLC cache misses, and sampling introduces frame pacing
jitter during the first minute of gameplay.

This patch disables autotuner sampling and keeps execution pinned to GMEM.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
index b918231..8271a90 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
@@ -100,6 +100,18 @@ tu_autotune_use_gmem(struct tu_autotune *at,
                      struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer,
                      const struct tu_render_pass *pass)
 {
+   /* Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 (SM8635 / Adreno 735):
+    * Disable runtime autotuner experimentation.
+    * Pin decisions strictly to GMEM tiling to prevent memory bus choke
+    * and eliminate frame pacing spikes from counter sampling.
+    */
+   if (cmd_buffer->device->physical_device->info->chip >= 7) {
+      return true;
+   }
+
    if (!at || !at->enabled)
       return tu_render_pass_use_gmem(pass, cmd_buffer->state.framebuffer);
 
